num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** On a series-trust platform (e.g., the Foreside/ACA-affiliated distributor, Quasar, Northern Lights), the principal underwriter is mainly a **legal and operational role**. It is the FINRA-registered broker-dealer named in the trust's distribution agreement. It reviews marketing materials under FINRA Rule 2210, processes authorized-participant creation and redemption paperwork, and supports registration obligations. It does **not**, by itself, provide wholesalers, a sales force or asset inflows.\n\n**Asset gathering is usually contracted separately**, through:\n- the adviser's own sales team\n- third-party marketing or wholesaling firms\n- paid platform or \"shelf\" access and revenue-sharing with intermediaries (wirehouses, RIA custodians, model marketplaces)\n- capital-markets and lead-market-maker support\n\n**Packages differ.** Some white-label providers bundle distribution, marketing and capital-markets help, often for extra fees. Others are compliance-only. Sponsors should check contracts and fee schedules. Winning intermediary-platform approval and generating flows remain the adviser's job.","ttft_ms":1522,"type":"result","duration_ms":4053,"uuid":"14ebb5c5-91ae-45ac-949e-70fbe37da540","ttft_stream_ms":1331,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1331,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
